WEBVTT

00:00:08.593 --> 00:00:10.136
[bangs]

00:00:12.722 --> 00:00:14.140
[Kitty] You know what?

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:18.019
I love the red ones.

00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:19.312
Is it cherry?

00:00:19.938 --> 00:00:21.773
Is it strawberry? I'm not really sure.

00:00:21.856 --> 00:00:24.150
I can never tell.

00:00:24.776 --> 00:00:26.653
It's kind of like people, you know?

00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:29.697
You think they're one thing,

00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:33.952
but it turns out they're
something else entirely.

00:00:37.288 --> 00:00:38.373
Diane.

00:00:38.456 --> 00:00:40.458
[gasps] She knows.

00:00:40.542 --> 00:00:42.335
[Kitty] Can you imagine if this got out?

00:00:43.378 --> 00:00:47.090
The governor's secret past
as the Crimson Paw? Whoo.

00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:48.758
Talk about a scandal.

00:00:49.592 --> 00:00:51.803
She will be in the hot bubble water.

00:00:53.638 --> 00:00:54.722
So...

00:00:56.808 --> 00:00:59.519
Let me rephrase the question.

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:04.566
Play along, and Diane's secret is safe.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.822
Or don't, and you, Diane,
the good life...

00:01:10.905 --> 00:01:14.409
it all comes crashing down.

00:01:15.451 --> 00:01:16.536
What'll it be?

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.833
[sighs]

00:01:22.709 --> 00:01:25.503
All right, hot sauce. What's the job?

00:01:33.845 --> 00:01:35.513
That's the job.

00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:37.181
[Snake] Whoa.

00:01:37.265 --> 00:01:38.266
Wow.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.351
[Wolf whistles]

00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:42.395
That's the MoonX rocket!

00:01:42.478 --> 00:01:44.480
[dramatic music playing]

00:01:48.026 --> 00:01:49.068
Seriously?

00:01:49.152 --> 00:01:50.612
[Doom] You better believe it, girl.

00:01:50.695 --> 00:01:53.865
Why steal a car when you can steal
a big, jumbo rocket ship?

00:01:54.449 --> 00:01:55.700
I think she's serious.

00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:57.410
Why would you wanna steal a rocket?

00:01:57.493 --> 00:02:00.079
A heist is never just about the loot.

00:02:00.163 --> 00:02:02.123
Isn't that right, Wolf?

00:02:02.206 --> 00:02:03.625
It's a power move.

00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:05.960
Exactly. You get it.

00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:07.754
-He gets it.
-[Pigtail chuckles]

00:02:07.837 --> 00:02:09.797
All right, now, come on.
We got work to do.

00:02:10.965 --> 00:02:12.550
And after that, we're square, right?

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.135
You're gonna give us the video?

00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:16.346
-Thieves' honor.
-[Doom chuckles]

00:02:16.429 --> 00:02:18.139
This is gonna be gnarly.

00:02:18.222 --> 00:02:19.515
In the good way.

00:02:20.016 --> 00:02:21.893
[Kitty] Come on, y'all.
We're going on a hike.

00:02:21.976 --> 00:02:24.562
So are we bad again, or...

00:02:25.188 --> 00:02:26.606
You gotta hand it to 'em.

00:02:26.689 --> 00:02:28.608
They thought of almost everything.

00:02:28.691 --> 00:02:29.859
Almost?

00:02:29.942 --> 00:02:32.070
Oh. You got an angle!

00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:34.155
[scoffs] I've always got an angle.

00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:36.616
One last job and after that,

00:02:36.699 --> 00:02:39.911
Little Miss Lollipop's gonna
regret she ever met us.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.000
[knocking]

00:02:46.084 --> 00:02:47.543
[buzzer sounds]

00:02:48.461 --> 00:02:49.754
Madam Governor?

00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:51.381
Take me to his cell.

00:02:52.382 --> 00:02:53.675
[inmate] Oh, baby.

00:02:54.342 --> 00:02:55.760
[inmate howls]

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.055
[thunder rumbling]

00:03:00.723 --> 00:03:02.934
Well, well, well.

00:03:03.768 --> 00:03:05.228
Hello, Diane.

00:03:05.853 --> 00:03:07.146
Marmalade.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.359
Of all the super maximum prisons
in all the world,

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:14.570
you had to walk into mine.

00:03:14.654 --> 00:03:16.447
Oh, my. [clears throat]

00:03:16.531 --> 00:03:18.408
You look like a balloon animal.

00:03:18.491 --> 00:03:19.742
I know, right?

00:03:19.826 --> 00:03:21.035
Today was arm day.

00:03:21.119 --> 00:03:23.246
That's why I'm looking extra swole.

00:03:24.038 --> 00:03:27.667
So, to what do I owe the visit?

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.129
I wonder if it has anything
to do with your mangy protégés

00:03:31.212 --> 00:03:32.588
fleeing the scene of a crime.

00:03:32.672 --> 00:03:34.632
How do you know about that?

00:03:34.716 --> 00:03:36.300
It's my job to know.

00:03:36.384 --> 00:03:39.220
I'm the editor in chief
of the Crazy Max Chronicle.

00:03:39.303 --> 00:03:41.681
I also do yearbook,
and I'm captain of the pickleball team.

00:03:41.764 --> 00:03:43.474
To be honest,
I'm kinda crushing it in here.

00:03:43.558 --> 00:03:44.892
All right, well, good for you.

00:03:44.976 --> 00:03:47.812
But what do you know about MacGuffinite?

00:03:47.895 --> 00:03:49.188
Oh.

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:51.357
MacGuffinium Fictitium.

00:03:51.441 --> 00:03:53.568
[stool squeaking]

00:03:53.651 --> 00:03:55.445
Fascinating metal.

00:03:55.528 --> 00:03:57.989
With one extremely unique property.

00:04:00.324 --> 00:04:01.409
And that is?

00:04:01.492 --> 00:04:03.619
Well, I'm not just gonna tell you, am I?

00:04:03.703 --> 00:04:04.746
Did you forget?

00:04:04.829 --> 00:04:07.123
I'm sitting in prison for your crimes.

00:04:07.206 --> 00:04:09.625
So what's in it for me?

00:04:09.709 --> 00:04:12.003
I am not giving you a pardon.

00:04:12.086 --> 00:04:13.880
[scoffs, laughs] A pardon?

00:04:13.963 --> 00:04:15.423
In the middle of pickleball season?

00:04:15.506 --> 00:04:18.176
No. I have a better idea.

00:04:19.135 --> 00:04:22.805
How would you like to play a game?

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:25.016
What sort of sick game do you want me to--

00:04:26.976 --> 00:04:28.895
Backstabbing governors first.

00:04:28.978 --> 00:04:30.271
[sighs]

00:04:31.147 --> 00:04:32.315
Oh, goody!

00:04:35.276 --> 00:04:36.903
[Kitty] A/I right, everyone, listen up.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.364
Each of you has a specific part to play.

00:04:40.907 --> 00:04:42.116
-[grunts]
-[laughs]

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.367
[grunts]

00:04:43.451 --> 00:04:45.119
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

00:04:45.203 --> 00:04:46.704
Safecracking gear!

00:04:46.788 --> 00:04:47.955
Disguises!

00:04:48.456 --> 00:04:50.082
[computer voice] Welcome, Ms. Tarantula.

00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:51.959
That is some serious tech.

00:04:52.043 --> 00:04:53.586
Uh, I think I got the wrong bag.

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:56.672
Yeah, this doesn't seem like proper attire
to infiltrate a launch site.

00:04:56.756 --> 00:04:58.132
[chuckles] Oh, no.

00:04:58.216 --> 00:04:59.884
We're not going to the launch site.

00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:02.637
We found a way to circumvent
every level of security

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:03.888
leading to the rocket,

00:05:03.971 --> 00:05:05.973
and it's right there on Mr. Moon's wrist.

00:05:06.057 --> 00:05:09.393
[Pigtail] Watch controls
everything from front gate,

00:05:09.477 --> 00:05:10.728
<i>to mission control,</i>

00:05:11.604 --> 00:05:12.647
<i>to blast-off.</i>

00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:18.236
Steal the watch, steal the rocket.

00:05:18.319 --> 00:05:20.571
Only problem? He never takes it off.

00:05:20.655 --> 00:05:23.324
Lucky we have
world-famous pickpocket.

00:05:23.407 --> 00:05:25.034
And we think there's a window.

00:05:25.117 --> 00:05:26.369
"Jeremiah Moon invites you

00:05:26.452 --> 00:05:28.663
to his exclusive,
state-of-the-art wedding."

00:05:28.746 --> 00:05:30.540
Are you serious?
We're gonna crash the wedding?

00:05:30.623 --> 00:05:32.667
Oh. I love weddings!

00:05:33.543 --> 00:05:34.877
I mean, you know-- [scoffs]

00:05:34.961 --> 00:05:36.546
[stammering] I-- I mean, I like 'em.

00:05:36.629 --> 00:05:38.089
They're fine. I don't care.

00:05:38.172 --> 00:05:39.841
Whatever. No one cares.

00:05:39.924 --> 00:05:41.425
Um...

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:42.760
Here's how it's gonna go.

00:05:42.844 --> 00:05:44.720
[thrilling music playing]

00:05:45.221 --> 00:05:49.183
[Kitty] 7his is a highly exclusive event,
and it's got protection fo match.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.602
<i>Doom) So, we'll have to get creative.</i>

00:05:51.686 --> 00:05:53.604
-[muffled groans]
-I'm a little rusty

00:05:53.688 --> 00:05:56.274
but I promise to play you respectfully.

00:05:56.941 --> 00:05:59.068
[Italian accent] Mamma mia,
where's my flowers?

00:05:59.151 --> 00:06:01.779
Pregol Cappuccino! Extra grande

00:06:01.863 --> 00:06:04.031
Tutti-frutti. Limoncello.

00:06:04.115 --> 00:06:07.201
Oh, the veil? It's vintage.
A princess wore it.

